{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/skiplists"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SkipLists\/documentation\/SkipLists"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SkipLists\/documentation\/SkipLists\/SkipList"],"title":"Sorted sets","anchor":"Sorted-sets"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SkipLists\/documentation\/SkipLists\/SkipList","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is a sorted set kept in a skip list (Pugh, 1990): sorted linked lists stacked in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"levels, each level a random sample of the one below, searched from the top level down. Each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element’s tower gains a level with probability 1\/4, so lookup, insertion and removal take"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O(log "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":") expected time with no rebalancing. Its elements are a random-access collection in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ascending order, indexed by rank, with "},{"code":"lowerBound(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"upperBound(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"elements(in:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":";"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the API matches the sorted sets of "},{"code":"BinarySearchTrees","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import SkipLists","","var numbers: SkipList = [8, 3, 5, 1, 9]","numbers.insert(4)","numbers.contains(2)     \/\/ false","numbers.lowerBound(5)   \/\/ 3, the index of 5"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The tower heights come from a random number generator given at creation; a seeded one makes every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"list reproducible. The list’s levels are a directed acyclic graph, which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SkipLists\/documentation\/SkipLists\/SkipList\/layersView-swift.property","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" exposes to Grafluent’s algorithms and drawings as a "},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(import Grafluent’s "},{"code":"GraphProtocols","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" module beside this one): a vertex for each element on each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"level of its tower, an edge along each level and an edge down each tower."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"title":"SkipLists","externalID":"SkipLists","symbolKind":"module","role":"collection","roleHeading":"Framework","modules":[{"name":"SkipLists"}]},"abstract":[{"text":"Skip lists as sorted sets, with their levels as a directed graph.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://SkipLists/documentation/SkipLists/SkipList/layersView-swift.property":{"kind":"symbol","title":"layersView","conformance":{"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Element"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Comparable"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}]},"url":"\/documentation\/skiplists\/skiplist\/layersview-swift.property","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"layersView","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:9SkipLists0A4ListV","text":"SkipList","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">.","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:9SkipLists0A4ListVAASHRzrlE10LayersViewV","text":"LayersView","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The list’s levels as a directed graph: a vertex for each element on each level of its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tower, an edge from each to the next element on the same level, and an edge from each down","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to the same element on the level below. The head is not a vertex.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SkipLists\/documentation\/SkipLists\/SkipList\/layersView-swift.property"},"doc://SkipLists/documentation/SkipLists/SkipList":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A sorted set kept in a skip list: sorted linked lists stacked in levels, each level a random"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sample of the one below, searched from the top level down (Pugh, 1990)."}],"url":"\/documentation\/skiplists\/skiplist","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SkipList","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SkipLists\/documentation\/SkipLists\/SkipList","title":"SkipList","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SkipList","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://SkipLists/documentation/SkipLists":{"type":"topic","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/SkipLists\/documentation\/SkipLists","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Skip lists as sorted sets, with their levels as a directed graph."}],"title":"SkipLists","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/skiplists"}}}